<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 52,593 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 52,593 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 52,593 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7.00 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday compared to 63,258 tonnes in the same period on Sunday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>						Sunday	September 8</p>
<p>    Export cargo			   8,660	3,485</p>
<p>    Import cargo			  43,933     59,773</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and eight berthed. In the next 24 hours, three were expected to sail and 10 were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Jet oil		  25,000	 Sand Gate	     9/9</p>
<p>Sugar		     7,500	 Mehediniti	   10/9</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Maribell	     10/9</p>
<p>Palm oil		 23,000	 Antea		  11/9</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
